<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE AGAIN.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE AGAIN.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Tuesday it will cut its retail prices for diesel in the Netherlands by 1.8 cents per litre with effect from November 7.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said. It had already cut the diesel price by two cents per litre with effect from November 4. In both cases gasoline prices remained unchanged.</p>
<p>From Thursday the price of diesel at Shell's self-service stations goes down to 1.482 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
